Z||000002||theogre||12-19-2000||07:13 PM||||If the 85 has the ajar switch on the latch, and I think it does, then read my cave article. It's in the options section. tells you everything you want to know.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Bob Englert||12-19-2000||07:37 PM||||If I remember correctly the wiring harness connector at the decklid hinge is different between the 85 and the 88.  I think it is related to the ajar switch in in the body (a plunger switch) in the 85 and it is in the latch itself (decklid side) in the Formula.<P>If the decklid latch and key is good in the 85 you can probably just swap the latch and key lock to the new decklid.  You will also need to take the release wiring out of the old decklid and install it in the Formula lid.<P>Should be fairly easy to do.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000004||Phil||12-19-2000||08:18 PM||||Don't forget to either change or adjust the springs. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||fiero56||12-19-2000||09:55 PM||||Hey Dave. Watcha' doing with the '85 decklid? ||||reg||1
